%description:

Tcp.stopOperationTimeout:waits -- host1 sends a FIN at the stop, and the stage ends when its ACK arrives at 1.4 s.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the stop of the node: the longest wait for the connections; each
connection that its application left open gets the CLOSE call of RFC 9293 (a FIN), and the stage
of TCP ends when each connection has its data and FIN acknowledged [...], or at this timeout
[...]. 0s: the connections end at once, without a segment".

The classes: zero (0s: the stage of TCP deletes the connections at once, without a
segment), waits (a positive value, 2s the default: each connection that its application left
open gets a FIN, and the stage ends when each connection has its FIN acknowledged) and expires
(a value that the peer does not meet: the stage ends at the timeout and deletes the
connections). The code: Tcp::handleStopOperation() issues the CLOSE call of RFC 9293 section
3.10.4 to each connection that is still open (Tcp::closeConnectionsForStop()), and
delayActiveOperationFinish() waits while a connection is in SYN_RCVD, ESTABLISHED, CLOSE_WAIT,
FIN_WAIT_1, CLOSING or LAST_ACK; Tcp::connectionStateChanged() checks the connections at each
change of their states, and the timeout ends the wait through the crash handler. During the
wait, Tcp drops what it would send to the applications, which are down already. This test separates "waits" from the other classes.

Host under test: host1; host1 has a TcpTestApp, which connects to host2 at 0.1 s and never closes the connection, also
not at the stop: TcpTestApp takes no part in the lifecycle. The link delay is 100 ms, so the
round trip is 400 ms. host2 sends a ping to host1 every 50 ms from 0.525 s on, so the ping n
leaves at 0.525 s + n * 50 ms and reaches host1 200 ms later. The tester stops host1 at 1.0 s;
the network layer of host1 goes down, and stops to answer pings, when the stage of TCP ends. Observation: level 1, host1 sends a FIN at the stop, and the stage ends when its ACK arrives at 1.4 s; host2 sees the FIN 200 ms after it
leaves, because the stop sends it inside the action of the tester. The last reply that host2
gets is the reply to the ping 13 (1.175 s), whose request reached host1 before the end of the
stage at 1.4 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.stopOperationTimeout
%# class: waits
%# value: 2s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.stopOperationTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpStopOperationTimeoutWaits")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000); })
                 .describe("host1 connects to host2; its application never closes the connection"))
        .once(on("host2.app[1]").signal("pingRxSeq")
             .filterValue(0)
             .describe("the reply to the first ping")
             .within(1.0))
        .act(action().at(1.0).stopNode("host1").describe("stop host1"))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.finBit == true")
             .describe("the FIN of the connection that the application left open, at host2")
             .within(0.3))
        .once(on("host2.app[1]").signal("pingRxSeq")
             .filterValue(13)
             .describe("the reply to the ping 13, sent at 1.175 s")
             .within(0.385))
        .never(on("host2.app[1]").signal("pingRxSeq")
              .filterValueAtLeast(14)
              .describe("a reply after the end of the stage of TCP")
              .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpStopOperationTimeoutWaits compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.stopOperationTimeout = 2s    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 100ms
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host2.numApps = 2
*.host2.app[1].typename = "PingApp"
*.host2.app[1].destAddr = "host1"
*.host2.app[1].startTime = 0.525s
*.host2.app[1].sendInterval = 0.05s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpStopOperationTimeoutWaits: PASS
